        "laureates": [
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov",
          "Daniel J. Drucker"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative therapies for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B029",
    "B024"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B014 most convincingly joins a durable physiological discovery to mature, broad therapeutic benefit in diabetes and obesity. Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker provide a coherent three-person configuration for the GLP-1 physiological account and its therapeutic enabling role, provided that the citation is kept tightly bounded and does not purport to credit the full pharmaceutical, clinical, or implementation pathway.",
    "case_against": "Attribution for B014 remains the central limitation: peptide biology, drug design, pharmaceutical development, and clinical investigation extend beyond the proposed three names. B029 has more direct preventive consequences and B024 has a particularly enduring foundational framework with a compact proposed pair. The supplied discussion does not resolve all historical-credit questions for any of these configurations.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson favors B029 because HPV virus-like-particle vaccines combine a bounded preventive discovery with mature population-level medical benefit, while regarding GLP-1 attribution as distributed.",
        "response": "I accept that B029 is an outstanding alternative and that its preventive achievement is exceptionally compelling. Its own discussion, however, leaves necessary resolution of roles in antigen design, particle assembly, and translation, and population outcomes are partly conditioned by access, uptake, screening, and follow-up. B014 likewise requires narrow framing, but its proposed laureates remain coherent for GLP-1 physiology rather than the entire therapeutic-development enterprise."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann favors B037 for its compact Mori-Walter attribution and mature fundamental mechanism, while questioning whether GLP-1 translation can be represented adequately by three people.",
        "response": "The compactness and mechanistic depth of B037 are substantial strengths. I continue to give greater weight to the direct, established therapeutic consequences of B014, while agreeing that its citation must distinguish physiological discovery from the wider translational pathway. The less settled disease-specific therapeutic causality for B037 remains relevant in this comparison."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius favors B024 as a foundational, enduring framework for adaptive immunity with Miller and Cooper as a delimited pair, while identifying a possible eligibility and historical-boundary concern.",
        "response": "B024 remains my leading foundational alternative. Its conceptual and medical importance is beyond question within the supplied record, but the unresolved eligibility concern and selective historical boundary should not be ignored. B014 offers an equally well-matured physiological principle together with unusually direct therapeutic consequences, subject to the attribution qualification stated above."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker can be defined as the indispensable three-person attribution for the specified GLP-1 physiological achievement after separating it from broader drug-development and clinical contributions.",
      "Whether the unresolved eligibility and historical-boundary questions for B024, or the historical allocation questions for B029, would alter their comparative standing after further review."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
